{
  "info": {
    "name": "Store \u2014 Checkout & Rewards API",
    "description": "Uniblox assessment backend.\n\nStart the app first:\n    cd backend && ./mvnw spring-boot:run\n\n`Create cart` saves the new id into the `cartId` collection variable, so every\ncart request after it works without copy-pasting a UUID. `productId` defaults to 1.\n\nThese requests are an executable reference rather than a single sequential run.\nRelated requests do chain -- `Add item to cart` followed by `Add same product\nagain` shows that a repeat add increments the quantity instead of duplicating a\nrow -- but a cart is spent once it has been checked out, so scenarios after\ncheckout need a fresh cart. Run those individually, creating a new cart first,\nand set `couponCode` and `emptyCartId` for the requests that name them.\n\nImplemented through Phase 6B: products (read-only), cart create/retrieve,\nadd / update / remove cart items, idempotent checkout, order retrieval, and\nadministrative reward-coupon generation, coupon redemption at checkout, and the administrative report.\n\nCheckout requires an `Idempotency-Key` header. Repeating a checkout with the same\nkey returns the original order as 200 with `Idempotent-Replay: true`, rather than\ncreating a second one.\n\nErrors carry a stable `code` alongside the RFC 7807 fields, so several distinct\n409 conditions (CART_NOT_OPEN, CART_EMPTY, INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY) stay tellable apart.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "cartId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "emptyCartId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "idempotencyKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "couponCode",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
